diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..5648ceb 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -105,3 +105,43 @@ knife ssh 'hostname:fizzy-lb-*' 'sudo docker exec fizzy-load-balancer kamal-prox
 ## License
 
 fizzy-saas is released under the [O'Saasy License](LICENSE.md).
+
+### Billing configuration
+
+Hosted billing uses these environment variables (configure separately for each Stripe environment):
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`: server-side Stripe API key.
+* `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`: signing secret for this installation's webhook endpoint.
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID`: a recurring USD $20/month price (unlimited cards, 5 GB).
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID`: a recurring USD $25/month price (unlimited cards, 500 GB).
+
+Create the two monthly prices in Stripe and enable the hosted customer portal for
+payment method updates, cancellations, and switching between those prices. Configure
+Stripe to deliver `customer.subscription.created`, `customer.subscription.updated`,
+and `customer.subscription.deleted` to **`/stripe/webhooks`**, without an account
+prefix. For CLI forwarding use `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/stripe/webhooks`
+and use the signing secret printed by that command.
+
+Run the SaaS database migrations before deploying. Admins open billing from account
+settings. Checkout returns to the account's billing page; only a verified webhook
+activates a plan, not the browser redirect. Active, trialing, and past-due subscriptions
+retain their allowance (past-due is the payment-retry grace period); canceled, unpaid,
+incomplete, and paused subscriptions fall back to Free. Duplicate webhook deliveries
+are ignored and older events cannot overwrite a newer subscription state.
+
+Free includes 1,000 published cards and 1 GB. Drafts don't consume the card allowance.
+Support staff can use `/admin/accounts` to comp an account (Unlimited+ allowance),
+uncomp it, or temporarily override measured card count and bytes used. Blank override
+fields use measured usage; Reset removes the override without touching subscriptions,
+waivers, or actual usage. Uncomp restores the account's subscribed plan, or Free.
+
+Offline billing regression tests (Stripe API calls are mocked, webhook signatures are real):
+
+```sh
+DATABASE_ADAPTER=sqlite bin/rails test \
+  saas/test/models/account/billing_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/card/card_limited_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/account/billings_controller_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/admin/accounts_controller_test.rb \
+  saas/test/controllers/stripe/webhooks_controller_test.rb
+```
diff --git a/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb b/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb
